  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A radioactive sample has a decay constant <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span> (measured in <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\mathrm{s}^{-1}\"></span>). Which of the following expressions represents the time, in seconds, required for the activity of the sample to decrease to one-tenth of its initial activity?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{10\\lambda}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\ln 10}{\\lambda}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\ln 2}{10\\lambda}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{\\lambda}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
